# Firefox AMO Upload

Sign with `./release.sh`, which reads `./amo-credentials.local` (on PC this is a symlink to `~/proj/mybrowser/amo-credentials.local`).

Full credential policy: `mybrowser/docs/amo-credentials.md`.

## Command

```bash
./release.sh            # zip + listed submit
./release.sh --zip-only # zip only
./release.sh --lint     # web-ext lint
```

`release.sh` already excludes `chrome/` and gitignored creds. Set `block_until_ms` to **120000**.

## If AMO rejects the JWT

Copy `amo-credentials.local` from hostname **PC** (`~/proj/mybrowser/amo-credentials.local`). Do **not** generate a new API key. A new key on this machine invalidates the copy on the other developer computers.

## Notes

- Extension id is `browser_specific_settings.gecko.id` in `manifest.json`.
- Bump the version **before** uploading (see version-bump rule).
- Never hardcode the JWT in rules or code.
- Listed channel. Release notes via `--amo-metadata` or the developer hub describe-version page.
